Imagine China has a big, important meeting where lots of people come together to talk about the rules and decisions for the country. This meeting is called the National People's Congress.

Think of it like a big family meeting where everyone gets to share ideas and decide what the family should do next. In China, this meeting helps make big decisions about laws and how the country should be run. It’s like a group of grown-ups sitting together to plan what happens next for everyone.

It’s not like a school class where everyone votes equally, but it’s a way for China to talk about what matters most and make choices together. [end of text]


